From 710ebb360b1fd79c5fb19a3bcdab6d8f405bf861 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luc3as <luc3as@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 17:04:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/25] Dashboard: edit a search, live status, price-drop marks
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Searches could be added and deleted but never changed, so fixing a typo in
an exclude list meant deleting the search and losing its history. Each row
now has an Edit form for everything but the URL (the URL is what the search
is; its listings and high-water mark hang off it). Query gains updated_at,
and the supervisor's restart signature includes it, so an edit reaches the
running poller on its next check without a process restart. A small form
sets every search's interval at once, for the "slow everything down while
the address cools off" moment.

The table now refreshes itself from /api/health every ten seconds — state,
last check, found count, error line — and shows an estimated next check
that counts down; nobody should have to reload a page to see whether the
thing is alive. The health payload gained the interval and last poll time
to support that. Listings whose price dropped are marked in the gallery
and sort by the time of the drop.
